{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790970229,"nonce":"A010kFsfcoDt9qp1TV8g+Z2SDGo=","title":"Method values have no identity: each evaluation is a fresh closure compared by address","message":"Row: Issue6705.\n\n`FunctionRef` codegen (codegen/cranelift_backend.rs) mallocs a new `{fn, null}` per evaluation and\n`make_closure` a new env holding `this`; `==` on function values is a raw pointer compare and\n`array_index_of` compares words, so `f == f` for the same method is false and `indexOf(method)`\nis -1. `Reflect.compareMethods` compares `{fn, env}` contents, so static methods pass and\nmember methods fail (env pointers differ). LLVM the same. Haxe eval itself gets member `==`\nfalse; static `==` and compareMethods(member) are true there.","files":null}]}